2. TECHNOLOGY AND PROJECT REQUIREMENTS

First, inspect the existing Google AI Studio project and determine which framework, dependencies, and file structure it currently uses.

If a project already exists, preserve its working framework and improve the existing project rather than unnecessarily rebuilding it from scratch.

If starting from scratch, choose a modern, Vercel-compatible implementation.

Preferred options:

* React with TypeScript and Vite, if creating a conventional client-rendered website.
* Next.js with TypeScript, if a full-stack framework is more appropriate.

Use the simplest architecture that reliably supports all the required features.

Do not mix incompatible framework configurations.

Use:

* TypeScript where appropriate.
* Reusable React components.
* Clean, maintainable code.
* Semantic HTML.
* Responsive CSS.
* Accessible forms and navigation.
* A consistent design system.
* Proper error handling.
* Working client-side navigation or framework-native routing.
* Production-ready asset paths.

